From 578e8bd29f57c787674e16107697227a543eb487 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mpaluri <mpaluri@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 13:49:53 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Program SCS descriptor to hostapd via SCS_CONFIGURE in NLHAL

Implements the SCS/MSCS QoS-management descriptor path for the nl80211
(OpenWrt, non-pwhm) AP HAL backend. On pwhm the descriptor is forwarded
through an Ambiorix RPC (handleQosMgmtDesc); OpenWrt has no pwhm, so the
descriptor is programmed directly to hostapd over the wpa_ctrl control
interface.

- ap_wlan_hal_nl80211.h: override supports_qos_management() -> true
  (gates the ap_manager call path) and declare
  handle_qos_management_descriptor().
- ap_wlan_hal_nl80211.cpp: include beerocks_string_utils.h and implement
  handle_qos_management_descriptor(): resolve BSSID -> vap_id -> per-BSS
  ifname, validate descriptor length (1..256) and qmid (<= 0xFF),
  hex-encode the descriptor, and send the raw wpa_ctrl command:
    SCS_CONFIGURE <peer_mac> <scs_sta_mac> <qm_id> <scs_desc_hex>

Signed-off-by: Gyanranjan Hazarika <gyanranj@qti.qualcomm.com>
Signed-off-by: Manaswini Paluri <mpaluri@qti.qualcomm.com>

diff --git a/agent/src/beerocks/fronthaul_manager/ap_manager/ap_manager.cpp b/agent/src/beerocks/fronthaul_manager/ap_manager/ap_manager.cpp
